[{"role": "system", "content": "\nYou are a programming expert. \nYou will be provided with a patch used to fix a bug. \n\nYour task is summarize the modifications made in the patch.\nYour summary should consist of two parts, modifications in each file and their relationships.\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "From 7e7c005b4b1f1f169bcc4b2c3a40085ecc663df2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Alexandre Belloni <alexandre.belloni@bootlin.com>\nDate: Mon, 21 Oct 2019 01:13:20 +0200\nSubject: [PATCH] rtc: disable uie before setting time and enable after\n\nWhen setting the time in the future with the uie timer enabled,\nrtc_timer_do_work will loop for a while because the expiration of the uie\ntimer was way before the current RTC time and a new timer will be enqueued\nuntil the current rtc time is reached.\n\nIf the uie timer is enabled, disable it before setting the time and enable\nit after expiring current timers (which may actually be an alarm).\n\nThis is the safest thing to do to ensure the uie timer is still\nsynchronized with the RTC, especially in the UIE emulation case.\n\nReported-by: syzbot+08116743f8ad6f9a6de7@syzkaller.appspotmail.com\nFixes: 6610e0893b8b (\"RTC: Rework RTC code to use timerqueue for events\")\nLink: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20191020231320.8191-1-alexandre.belloni@bootlin.com\nSigned-off-by: Alexandre Belloni <alexandre.belloni@bootlin.com>\n\ndiff --git a/drivers/rtc/interface.c b/drivers/rtc/interface.c\nindex eea700723976..f8b7c004d6ec 100644\n--- a/drivers/rtc/interface.c\n+++ b/drivers/rtc/interface.c\n@@ -125,7 +125,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(rtc_read_time);\n \n int rtc_set_time(struct rtc_device *rtc, struct rtc_time *tm)\n {\n-\tint err;\n+\tint err, uie;\n \n \terr = rtc_valid_tm(tm);\n \tif (err != 0)\n@@ -137,6 +137,17 @@ int rtc_set_time(struct rtc_device *rtc, struct rtc_time *tm)\n \n \trtc_subtract_offset(rtc, tm);\n \n+#ifdef CONFIG_RTC_INTF_DEV_UIE_EMUL\n+\tuie = rtc->uie_rtctimer.enabled || rtc->uie_irq_active;\n+#else\n+\tuie = rtc->uie_rtctimer.enabled;\n+#endif\n+\tif (uie) {\n+\t\terr = rtc_update_irq_enable(rtc, 0);\n+\t\tif (err)\n+\t\t\treturn err;\n+\t}\n+\n \terr = mutex_lock_interruptible(&rtc->ops_lock);\n \tif (err)\n \t\treturn err;\n@@ -153,6 +164,12 @@ int rtc_set_time(struct rtc_device *rtc, struct rtc_time *tm)\n \t/* A timer might have just expired */\n \tschedule_work(&rtc->irqwork);\n \n+\tif (uie) {\n+\t\terr = rtc_update_irq_enable(rtc, 1);\n+\t\tif (err)\n+\t\t\treturn err;\n+\t}\n+\n \ttrace_rtc_set_time(rtc_tm_to_time64(tm), err);\n \treturn err;\n }\n-- \n2.25.1\n\n\n\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "### Modifications in Each File\n\n**File: `drivers/rtc/interface.c`**\n1. **Variable Declaration**: A new variable `uie` is declared to track the status of the UIE (User Interrupt Event) timer.\n2. **UIE Status Check**: The code checks if the UIE timer is enabled or if the UIE IRQ is active, and assigns this status to the `uie` variable.\n3. **Disable UIE Timer**: If the UIE timer is enabled, the code disables it by calling `rtc_update_irq_enable(rtc, 0)`.\n4. **Enable UIE Timer**: After setting the RTC time and scheduling the work, the code re-enables the UIE timer by calling `rtc_update_irq_enable(rtc, 1)`.\n\n### Relationships Between Modifications\nThe modifications ensure that the UIE timer is disabled before the RTC time is set and re-enabled afterward. This sequence is crucial to prevent the `rtc_timer_do_work` function from looping unnecessarily when the UIE timer is set to expire before the current RTC time. By managing the UIE timer in this manner, the patch addresses synchronization issues between the UIE timer and the RTC, particularly in scenarios involving UIE emulation. This change is a direct response to the bug report and aims to enhance the reliability of the RTC time-setting process."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"llm_patch_file_names": ["drivers/rtc/interface.c"]}, "begin to deal with drivers/rtc/interface.c in strategy1", {"full_context_length": 54}, {"role": "system", "content": "You are a programming expert."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\n        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.\n        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.\n\n        Root cause:\n        The bug occurs when the UIE timer is enabled while setting the RTC time to a future value. This causes the `rtc_timer_do_work` function to loop indefinitely because the expiration of the UIE timer is set before the current RTC time, leading to a situation where a new timer is enqueued until the current RTC time is reached. This results in synchronization issues between the UIE timer and the RTC.\n        \n        Commit message:\n        rtc: disable uie before setting time and enable after\n\nWhen setting the time in the future with the uie timer enabled,\nrtc_timer_do_work will loop for a while because the expiration of the uie\ntimer was way before the current RTC time and a new timer will be enqueued\nuntil the current rtc time is reached.\n\nIf the uie timer is enabled, disable it before setting the time and enable\nit after expiring current timers (which may actually be an alarm).\n\nThis is the safest thing to do to ensure the uie timer is still\nsynchronized with the RTC, especially in the UIE emulation case.\n\nReported-by: syzbot+08116743f8ad6f9a6de7@syzkaller.appspotmail.com\nFixes: 6610e0893b8b (\"RTC: Rework RTC code to use timerqueue for events\")\nLink: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20191020231320.8191-1-alexandre.belloni@bootlin.com\nSigned-off-by: Alexandre Belloni <alexandre.belloni@bootlin.com>  \n        \n        Patch:\n         \n int rtc_set_time(struct rtc_device *rtc, struct rtc_time *tm)\n {\n-\tint err;\n+\tint err, uie;\n \n \terr = rtc_valid_tm(tm);\n \tif (err != 0)\n \t\treturn err;\n \n \terr = rtc_valid_range(rtc, tm);\n \tif (err)\n \t\treturn err;\n \n \trtc_subtract_offset(rtc, tm);\n \n+#ifdef CONFIG_RTC_INTF_DEV_UIE_EMUL\n+\tuie = rtc->uie_rtctimer.enabled || rtc->uie_irq_active;\n+#else\n+\tuie = rtc->uie_rtctimer.enabled;\n+#endif\n+\tif (uie) {\n+\t\terr = rtc_update_irq_enable(rtc, 0);\n+\t\tif (err)\n+\t\t\treturn err;\n+\t}\n+\n \terr = mutex_lock_interruptible(&rtc->ops_lock);\n \tif (err)\n \t\treturn err;\n \n \tif (!rtc->ops)\n \t\terr = -ENODEV;\n \telse if (rtc->ops->set_time)\n \t\terr = rtc->ops->set_time(rtc->dev.parent, tm);\n \telse\n \t\terr = -EINVAL;\n \n \tpm_stay_awake(rtc->dev.parent);\n \tmutex_unlock(&rtc->ops_lock);\n \t/* A timer might have just expired */\n \tschedule_work(&rtc->irqwork);\n \n+\tif (uie) {\n+\t\terr = rtc_update_irq_enable(rtc, 1);\n+\t\tif (err)\n+\t\t\treturn err;\n+\t}\n+\n \ttrace_rtc_set_time(rtc_tm_to_time64(tm), err);\n \treturn err;\n }\n EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(rtc_set_time);\n\n        \n        Provide a response strictly in the following format:\n        Code statements:\n        <text1>\n        <text2>\n        ...\n        <textN>\n    "}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Code statements:\n```c\nuie = rtc->uie_rtctimer.enabled || rtc->uie_irq_active;\nif (uie) {\n    err = rtc_update_irq_enable(rtc, 0);\n    if (err)\n        return err;\n}\n...\nif (uie) {\n    err = rtc_update_irq_enable(rtc, 1);\n    if (err)\n        return err;\n}\n```"}, {"s1_raw_stmts_infos": [{"buggy_stmt": "err = rtc_update_irq_enable(rtc, 0);", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 540, "induce_cid": "456d66ecd09e3bc326b93174745faafb6ac378d6"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (err)", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 115, "induce_cid": "6610e0893b8bc6f59b14fed7f089c5997f035f88"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (err)", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 135, "induce_cid": "4c4e5df1f346f70802bf4999de13d06dbbdf7a01"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (err)", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 141, "induce_cid": "0c86edc0d4970649f39748c4ce4f2895f728468f"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (err)", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 167, "induce_cid": "f44f7f96a20af16f6f12e1c995576d6becf5f57b"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (err)", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 256, "induce_cid": "f44f7f96a20af16f6f12e1c995576d6becf5f57b"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (err)", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 306, "induce_cid": "da96aea0ed177105cb13ee83b328f6c61e061d3f"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (err)", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 362, "induce_cid": "5548cbf7f148b9a039b19fa4697f1b9beaba2c78"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (err)", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 374, "induce_cid": "0c86edc0d4970649f39748c4ce4f2895f728468f"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (err)", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 399, "induce_cid": "0e36a9a4a788e4e92407774df76c545910810d35"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (err)", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 406, "induce_cid": "ca6dc2dab97133b874c2f6a76b6125497b67b429"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (err)", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 445, "induce_cid": "4c4e5df1f346f70802bf4999de13d06dbbdf7a01"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (err)", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 449, "induce_cid": "0c86edc0d4970649f39748c4ce4f2895f728468f"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (err)", "file_name": "drivers/rtc/interface.c", "lineno": 476, "induce_cid": "bd729d72b428261f2975360e0c1